      "statusChangeNewStatus": "needs more information",
      "value": "Hi あさると, thanks for your report! Your world was helpful in testing your issue.\n\nThis doesn't appear to be a bug with volume sliders. Setting the slider to 50% decreases the output by 10 dB, as expected. This makes the world sound half as loud as 100%.\n\n**However**, your world shows a valid issue in VRChat: World audio may exceed 0 dB, and if it does, users may not be able to use volume sliders as they expect.\n\nWe think that this could be solved by adding a limiter to VRChat's world volume output. This would prevent worlds from being **extremely** loud at 100%, which creators might only do on accident (or maliciously).\n\nHere's a Canny you might be interested in: https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/new-report-world-reason-loud-audio\n\nWould you like me to rename your post and change it into a feature request? Or would you prefer to make a new feature request and have this one closed?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
