  "details": "(The post title was edited after creation, see comments)\n\nVRChat Version:\n\n1277\n\nDescription of the bug:\n\nMultiple AudioSources will break the volume slider if the maximum world volume exceeds 0 dB.\n\nIf the volume exceeds 0 dB for some reason, the volume slider may not actually be set to 50% even if the volume is set to 50%, or it may be set to 10% and finally become equivalent to 100%.\n\nSteps to reproduce (how did you encounter the bug?):\n\nIt may be possible to reproduce this by simply setting the AudioSource so that the maximum volume exceeds 0 dB.\n\nIn my environment, I was able to reproduce this by simply placing two AudioSources that play music with a maximum volume of 0 dB.\n\nAny extra files? (output logs, screenshots):\n\nClip when the maximum volume is 0 dB: https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/881924651142479895/1071401111170318396/0dB.mp4\n\nabove 0dB : https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/881924651142479895/1071401113187782666/above_0dB.mp4\n\n(In this video, i placed four AudioSources with a maximum volume of 0 dB.)\n\nI'm created a world for volume slider test. please have Audacity or other tools available to monitor the volume.\n\ntest world: https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_fb865369-e380-4e4f-8766-e57e48838228",
